{"Success":true,"Data":{"State":"open","OpenTime":0,"CloseTime":0,"IsApproved":true,"IsPinned":false,"IsDeleted":false,"IsHidden":false,"IsArchived":false,"IsFollowing":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanReply":false,"CanFollow":true,"TotalPosts":24,"QueuedPosts":0,"DeletedPosts":0,"HasUnreadPosts":false,"HasAttachments":false,"Views":7031,"MovedTo":null,"MovedOn":0,"FirstPostId":1718682,"Rating":0,"RatingHits":0,"Starter":{"Id":242901,"Name":"cherany","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-242901.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":253,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"StartDate":1360476319,"LastPoster":{"Id":284536,"Name":"lorishultz2016","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":false},"PollState":"0","LastVote":0,"ForumId":74,"Preview":{"Id":1718682,"PostDate":1360476319,"PostContent":"With just 22 invites going out (half of those hand delivered), we had the luxury of being able t...","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"cheranymail@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1311875093,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-242901.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":253,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"cherany","Id":242901,"Name":"cherany","IsOnline":false}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":72470,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"840170d51db853c710c565cf3c88360b","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; With just 22 invites going out (half of those hand delivered), we had the luxury of being able to spend more per person and decided to go with the Message In a Bottle idea. &amp;nbsp;However, with all the super cute choices out there, I found myself wanting to incorporate other things, too. &amp;nbsp;In the end, I came up with a way to use all my favorite ideas: luggage tag, message in a bottle, passport, boarding pass, &amp;amp; suitcase!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Our STDs were luggage tag magnets, which I shared here:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186811\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186811\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186810\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186810\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Photographing the contents inside the bottle was difficult, but each bottle has blue sand, opalescent blue glass chips, pearly multi-colored shells, paper umbrella (various colors), and the invitation rolled up and tied with a ribbon sticking out of the cork. On the outside, I added the printed sticker, ribbon, and a charm.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1360471898649_3362\"&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186822\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186822\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Forgot to take my own pic, but found this image on the web; same charms we used (got them at Michael&#039;s).&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186820\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186820\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Paper umbrellas from Party City, colorful shells from Joanne, glass chips from Michael&#039;s. &amp;nbsp;(Blue sand also from Michael&#039;s, found beside a rainbow of colors on the kids&#039; craft aisle, not where the shells, starfish, and natural sand colors were. &amp;nbsp;We got our bottles from this site:&amp;nbsp;&lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186821\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186821\/width\/200\/height\/400\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Sticker designed in photoshop - let me know if you would like the .psd file, which can be pasted onto oval sticker templates (that&#039;s what we did).&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186809\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186809\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186819\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186819\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186818\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186818\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1360474245375_5214\"&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186835\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186835\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;span style=\"line-height: 1.231;\"&gt;I was lucky to find an image in Word for the actual invitations, since all the other graphic design aspects of this project were done the hard way by scouring the web for vector images (not easy - if anyone is looking for beach related vectors files, I now have several, many not shown here; let me know if you would like them, and I&#039;ll e-mail the files), then arranged into designs in Photoshop (super time consuming, can only recommend to complete control freaks\/picky designers).&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186814\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186814\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Box contains the bottle, card sleeve, and a passport booklet.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186815\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186815\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Inside the green sleeve is a Boarding Pass with event info &amp;amp; a Return Ticket for the RSVP card, which we put our address &amp;amp; a stamp on the back of, so people can mail it back like a postcard. &amp;nbsp; The sleeve is just a piece of cardstock tri-folded and tied with a ribbon.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186823\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186823\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186824\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186824\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Again, I used Photoshop to design these one element at a time, rather than from a template, but I can share the .psd layered files if anyone else is creating their designs with Photoshop. &amp;nbsp;Just let me know you want them, and I&#039;ll send.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186816\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186816\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; The passport was created by cutting and folding a pink cover from cardstock and gluing in individual pages. &amp;nbsp;I was absent minded and did not print on both sides of the pages, so I had to glue each page to the next, but that turned out to be a good thing, because it gave me a booklet to paste inside the pink cover as one piece. &amp;nbsp;I didn&#039;t take any pictures of the process, but if I&#039;m not making sense, feel free to ask questions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186817\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186817\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I designed the passport to be the same size as an actual passport, although I forget the exact dimensions (easy to google).&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186826\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186826\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Sticker designed in Photoshop; let me know if you&#039;d like the layered .psd file (everything you see is a separate element, and I have vector files for the images, if anyone wants those).&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Photoshop designs of each page:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186827\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186827\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186828\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186828\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186829\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186829\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186830\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186830\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186831\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186831\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186832\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186832\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186833\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186833\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186834\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186834\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Again, I have layered photoshop files of each page, if anyone wants them. &amp;nbsp;I added a border before printing, but they&#039;re otherwise exactly as I printed them. &amp;nbsp;This project taught me I really, really need to learn how to use some easier publishing programs! &amp;nbsp;Maybe one day when I&#039;m not so busy (like, after the wedding), I&#039;ll create some Word or Publisher files of these things to share here.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186812\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186812\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Contents all boxed up!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\" \" data-id=\"186813\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186813\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I meant them all to look the same, but I seriously underestimated how much ribbon I needed and had to make due with what the store had left when I ran out of pink mid-project. Ended up using green for our local friends (hand delivering those to save $) and pink for the long distance ones. &amp;nbsp;Trying not to let it bother me! &amp;nbsp;The ribbon is from Michael&#039;s and the boxes were purchased with our bottles (link provided under bottle pics). &amp;nbsp;I made the ribbon handle stiffer by gluing cardstock to the underside of it. Not sure how well they&#039;re going to hold up in the mail, but fingers crossed they still look like suitcases when they arrive in friends&#039; mailboxes!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; The finished product ended up weighing 12-13 ounces and was just under $4 to mail within the US. &amp;nbsp;One went to Canada for about $11 and two went further to the U.K. &amp;amp; Australia for nearly $17 each!&amp;nbsp;&lt;img id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1360474245375_5729\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/sad.gif\" style=\"line-height: 1.231;\" \/&gt;&amp;nbsp; Even still, I only spent about $75 mailing, since we have so many to hand deliver, so I wasn&#039;t too bothered by the International ones costing a fortune.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I&#039;m super excited to give these to friends! &amp;nbsp;Really proud of myself, but definitely glad to be done! &amp;nbsp;I lost track of the number of hours I worked on them (weeks!) and also of the cost (surely more than I&#039;d like to know, so I&#039;m happy to remain ignorant about it), but I do think they were worth all the effort. &amp;nbsp;I saved one to keep and will hopefully remember to bring it to Mexico to include in our pro photos.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1718682,"PostDate":1360476319,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> With just 22 invites going out (half of those hand delivered), we had the luxury of being able to spend more per person and decided to go with the Message In a Bottle idea. \u00a0However, with all the super cute choices out there, I found myself wanting to incorporate other things, too. \u00a0In the end, I came up with a way to use all my favorite ideas: luggage tag, message in a bottle, passport, boarding pass, & suitcase!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Our STDs were luggage tag magnets, which I shared here:<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186811\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186811\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186810\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186810\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Photographing the contents inside the bottle was difficult, but each bottle has blue sand, opalescent blue glass chips, pearly multi-colored shells, paper umbrella (various colors), and the invitation rolled up and tied with a ribbon sticking out of the cork. On the outside, I added the printed sticker, ribbon, and a charm.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1360471898649_3362\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186822\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186822\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Forgot to take my own pic, but found this image on the web; same charms we used (got them at Michael's).<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186820\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186820\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Paper umbrellas from Party City, colorful shells from Joanne, glass chips from Michael's. \u00a0(Blue sand also from Michael's, found beside a rainbow of colors on the kids' craft aisle, not where the shells, starfish, and natural sand colors were. \u00a0We got our bottles from this site:\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186821\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186821\/width\/200\/height\/400\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> Sticker designed in photoshop - let me know if you would like the .psd file, which can be pasted onto oval sticker templates (that's what we did).<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186809\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186809\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186819\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186819\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186818\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186818\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1360474245375_5214\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186835\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186835\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span>I was lucky to find an image in Word for the actual invitations, since all the other graphic design aspects of this project were done the hard way by scouring the web for vector images (not easy - if anyone is looking for beach related vectors files, I now have several, many not shown here; let me know if you would like them, and I'll e-mail the files), then arranged into designs in Photoshop (super time consuming, can only recommend to complete control freaks\/picky designers).<\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186814\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186814\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Box contains the bottle, card sleeve, and a passport booklet.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186815\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186815\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Inside the green sleeve is a Boarding Pass with event info & a Return Ticket for the RSVP card, which we put our address & a stamp on the back of, so people can mail it back like a postcard. \u00a0 The sleeve is just a piece of cardstock tri-folded and tied with a ribbon.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186823\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186823\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186824\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186824\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Again, I used Photoshop to design these one element at a time, rather than from a template, but I can share the .psd layered files if anyone else is creating their designs with Photoshop. \u00a0Just let me know you want them, and I'll send.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186816\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186816\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The passport was created by cutting and folding a pink cover from cardstock and gluing in individual pages. \u00a0I was absent minded and did not print on both sides of the pages, so I had to glue each page to the next, but that turned out to be a good thing, because it gave me a booklet to paste inside the pink cover as one piece. \u00a0I didn't take any pictures of the process, but if I'm not making sense, feel free to ask questions.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186817\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186817\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I designed the passport to be the same size as an actual passport, although I forget the exact dimensions (easy to google).<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186826\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186826\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Sticker designed in Photoshop; let me know if you'd like the layered .psd file (everything you see is a separate element, and I have vector files for the images, if anyone wants those).<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Photoshop designs of each page:<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186827\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186827\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186828\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186828\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186829\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186829\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186830\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186830\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186831\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186831\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186832\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186832\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186833\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186833\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186834\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186834\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Again, I have layered photoshop files of each page, if anyone wants them. \u00a0I added a border before printing, but they're otherwise exactly as I printed them. \u00a0This project taught me I really, really need to learn how to use some easier publishing programs! \u00a0Maybe one day when I'm not so busy (like, after the wedding), I'll create some Word or Publisher files of these things to share here.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186812\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186812\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Contents all boxed up!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186813\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186813\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I meant them all to look the same, but I seriously underestimated how much ribbon I needed and had to make due with what the store had left when I ran out of pink mid-project. Ended up using green for our local friends (hand delivering those to save $) and pink for the long distance ones. \u00a0Trying not to let it bother me! \u00a0The ribbon is from Michael's and the boxes were purchased with our bottles (link provided under bottle pics). \u00a0I made the ribbon handle stiffer by gluing cardstock to the underside of it. Not sure how well they're going to hold up in the mail, but fingers crossed they still look like suitcases when they arrive in friends' mailboxes!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The finished product ended up weighing 12-13 ounces and was just under $4 to mail within the US. \u00a0One went to Canada for about $11 and two went further to the U.K. & Australia for nearly $17 each!\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1360474245375_5729\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/sad.gif\" style=\"line-height: 1.231;\" \/><\/span>\u00a0 Even still, I only spent about $75 mailing, since we have so many to hand deliver, so I wasn't too bothered by the International ones costing a fortune.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I'm super excited to give these to friends! \u00a0Really proud of myself, but definitely glad to be done! \u00a0I lost track of the number of hours I worked on them (weeks!) and also of the cost (surely more than I'd like to know, so I'm happy to remain ignorant about it), but I do think they were worth all the effort. \u00a0I saved one to keep and will hopefully remember to bring it to Mexico to include in our pro photos.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"cheranymail@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1311875093,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-242901.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":253,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"cherany","Id":242901,"Name":"cherany","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":72470,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f8cd268fa21a2933ce7e043d052d480e","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; These are awesome. I love that you incorporated all the different elements of passport and message in a bottle. They are phenomenal! Don&#039;t let the diff colored ribbon bother you. I have had soooo many projects end up looking horrible, but I know how something small like that can irritate ya. Can&#039;t wait to see more of your creations!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1718863,"PostDate":1360520632,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> These are awesome. I love that you incorporated all the different elements of passport and message in a bottle. They are phenomenal! Don't let the diff colored ribbon bother you. I have had soooo many projects end up looking horrible, but I know how something small like that can irritate ya. Can't wait to see more of your creations!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"Enjoythepartykm@aol.com","IpAddress":"68.13.213.79","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1343393580,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-258455.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Tulumbride2013","Id":258455,"Name":"Tulumbride2013","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":72470,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"12592a0e7af2c1befecba8f0c78b1eec","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]cherany[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n With just 22 invites going out (half of those hand delivered), we had the luxury of being able to spend more per person and decided to go with the Message In a Bottle idea.  However, with all the super cute choices out there, I found myself wanting to incorporate other things, too.  In the end, I came up with a way to use all my favorite ideas: luggage tag, message in a bottle, passport, boarding pass, &amp;amp; suitcase! \n \n Our STDs were luggage tag magnets, which I shared here: \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186811\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186810\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n Photographing the contents inside the bottle was difficult, but each bottle has blue sand, opalescent blue glass chips, pearly multi-colored shells, paper umbrella (various colors), and the invitation rolled up and tied with a ribbon sticking out of the cork. On the outside, I added the printed sticker, ribbon, and a charm. \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186822\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n Forgot to take my own pic, but found this image on the web; same charms we used (got them at Michael&#039;s). \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186820\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n Paper umbrellas from Party City, colorful shells from Joanne, glass chips from Michael&#039;s.  (Blue sand also from Michael&#039;s, found beside a rainbow of colors on the kids&#039; craft aisle, not where the shells, starfish, and natural sand colors were.  We got our bottles from this site: [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186821\/width\/200\/height\/400[\/img] \n Sticker designed in photoshop - let me know if you would like the .psd file, which can be pasted onto oval sticker templates (that&#039;s what we did). \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186809\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186819\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186818\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186835\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n I was lucky to find an image in Word for the actual invitations, since all the other graphic design aspects of this project were done the hard way by scouring the web for vector images (not easy - if anyone is looking for beach related vectors files, I now have several, many not shown here; let me know if you would like them, and I&#039;ll e-mail the files), then arranged into designs in Photoshop (super time consuming, can only recommend to complete control freaks\/picky designers). \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186814\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n Box contains the bottle, card sleeve, and a passport booklet. \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186815\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n Inside the green sleeve is a Boarding Pass with event info &amp;amp; a Return Ticket for the RSVP card, which we put our address &amp;amp; a stamp on the back of, so people can mail it back like a postcard.   The sleeve is just a piece of cardstock tri-folded and tied with a ribbon. \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186823\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186824\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n Again, I used Photoshop to design these one element at a time, rather than from a template, but I can share the .psd layered files if anyone else is creating their designs with Photoshop.  Just let me know you want them, and I&#039;ll send. \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186816\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n The passport was created by cutting and folding a pink cover from cardstock and gluing in individual pages.  I was absent minded and did not print on both sides of the pages, so I had to glue each page to the next, but that turned out to be a good thing, because it gave me a booklet to paste inside the pink cover as one piece.  I didn&#039;t take any pictures of the process, but if I&#039;m not making sense, feel free to ask questions.  \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186817\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n I designed the passport to be the same size as an actual passport, although I forget the exact dimensions (easy to google). \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186826\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n Sticker designed in Photoshop; let me know if you&#039;d like the layered .psd file (everything you see is a separate element, and I have vector files for the images, if anyone wants those). \n \n Photoshop designs of each page: \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186827\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186828\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186829\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186830\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186831\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186832\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186833\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186834\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n Again, I have layered photoshop files of each page, if anyone wants them.  I added a border before printing, but they&#039;re otherwise exactly as I printed them.  This project taught me I really, really need to learn how to use some easier publishing programs!  Maybe one day when I&#039;m not so busy (like, after the wedding), I&#039;ll create some Word or Publisher files of these things to share here. \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186812\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n Contents all boxed up! \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186813\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n I meant them all to look the same, but I seriously underestimated how much ribbon I needed and had to make due with what the store had left when I ran out of pink mid-project. Ended up using green for our local friends (hand delivering those to save $) and pink for the long distance ones.  Trying not to let it bother me!  The ribbon is from Michael&#039;s and the boxes were purchased with our bottles (link provided under bottle pics).  I made the ribbon handle stiffer by gluing cardstock to the underside of it. Not sure how well they&#039;re going to hold up in the mail, but fingers crossed they still look like suitcases when they arrive in friends&#039; mailboxes! \n \n The finished product ended up weighing 12-13 ounces and was just under $4 to mail within the US.  One went to Canada for about $11 and two went further to the U.K. &amp;amp; Australia for nearly $17 each! [img]http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/sad.gif[\/img]  Even still, I only spent about $75 mailing, since we have so many to hand deliver, so I wasn&#039;t too bothered by the International ones costing a fortune. \n \n I&#039;m super excited to give these to friends!  Really proud of myself, but definitely glad to be done!  I lost track of the number of hours I worked on them (weeks!) and also of the cost (surely more than I&#039;d like to know, so I&#039;m happy to remain ignorant about it), but I do think they were worth all the effort.  I saved one to keep and will hopefully remember to bring it to Mexico to include in our pro photos.[\/quote] \n Wow, these are amazing!! You can tell a lot of time and effort went into these and they are very personalized!","Attachments":[],"Id":1718876,"PostDate":1360521532,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>cherany<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> With just 22 invites going out (half of those hand delivered), we had the luxury of being able to spend more per person and decided to go with the Message In a Bottle idea. \u00a0However, with all the super cute choices out there, I found myself wanting to incorporate other things, too. \u00a0In the end, I came up with a way to use all my favorite ideas: luggage tag, message in a bottle, passport, boarding pass, & suitcase!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Our STDs were luggage tag magnets, which I shared here:<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186811\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186811\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186810\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186810\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Photographing the contents inside the bottle was difficult, but each bottle has blue sand, opalescent blue glass chips, pearly multi-colored shells, paper umbrella (various colors), and the invitation rolled up and tied with a ribbon sticking out of the cork. On the outside, I added the printed sticker, ribbon, and a charm.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1360471898649_3362\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186822\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186822\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Forgot to take my own pic, but found this image on the web; same charms we used (got them at Michael's).<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186820\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186820\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Paper umbrellas from Party City, colorful shells from Joanne, glass chips from Michael's. \u00a0(Blue sand also from Michael's, found beside a rainbow of colors on the kids' craft aisle, not where the shells, starfish, and natural sand colors were. \u00a0We got our bottles from this site:\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186821\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186821\/width\/200\/height\/400\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> Sticker designed in photoshop - let me know if you would like the .psd file, which can be pasted onto oval sticker templates (that's what we did).<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186809\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186809\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186819\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186819\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186818\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186818\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1360474245375_5214\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186835\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186835\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span>I was lucky to find an image in Word for the actual invitations, since all the other graphic design aspects of this project were done the hard way by scouring the web for vector images (not easy - if anyone is looking for beach related vectors files, I now have several, many not shown here; let me know if you would like them, and I'll e-mail the files), then arranged into designs in Photoshop (super time consuming, can only recommend to complete control freaks\/picky designers).<\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186814\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186814\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Box contains the bottle, card sleeve, and a passport booklet.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186815\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186815\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Inside the green sleeve is a Boarding Pass with event info & a Return Ticket for the RSVP card, which we put our address & a stamp on the back of, so people can mail it back like a postcard. \u00a0 The sleeve is just a piece of cardstock tri-folded and tied with a ribbon.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186823\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186823\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186824\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186824\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Again, I used Photoshop to design these one element at a time, rather than from a template, but I can share the .psd layered files if anyone else is creating their designs with Photoshop. \u00a0Just let me know you want them, and I'll send.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186816\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186816\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The passport was created by cutting and folding a pink cover from cardstock and gluing in individual pages. \u00a0I was absent minded and did not print on both sides of the pages, so I had to glue each page to the next, but that turned out to be a good thing, because it gave me a booklet to paste inside the pink cover as one piece. \u00a0I didn't take any pictures of the process, but if I'm not making sense, feel free to ask questions.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186817\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186817\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I designed the passport to be the same size as an actual passport, although I forget the exact dimensions (easy to google).<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186826\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186826\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Sticker designed in Photoshop; let me know if you'd like the layered .psd file (everything you see is a separate element, and I have vector files for the images, if anyone wants those).<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Photoshop designs of each page:<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186827\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186827\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186828\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186828\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186829\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186829\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186830\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186830\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186831\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186831\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186832\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186832\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186833\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186833\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186834\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186834\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Again, I have layered photoshop files of each page, if anyone wants them. \u00a0I added a border before printing, but they're otherwise exactly as I printed them. \u00a0This project taught me I really, really need to learn how to use some easier publishing programs! \u00a0Maybe one day when I'm not so busy (like, after the wedding), I'll create some Word or Publisher files of these things to share here.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186812\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186812\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Contents all boxed up!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\" \" data-id=\"186813\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/186813\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I meant them all to look the same, but I seriously underestimated how much ribbon I needed and had to make due with what the store had left when I ran out of pink mid-project. Ended up using green for our local friends (hand delivering those to save $) and pink for the long distance ones. \u00a0Trying not to let it bother me! \u00a0The ribbon is from Michael's and the boxes were purchased with our bottles (link provided under bottle pics). \u00a0I made the ribbon handle stiffer by gluing cardstock to the underside of it. Not sure how well they're going to hold up in the mail, but fingers crossed they still look like suitcases when they arrive in friends' mailboxes!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The finished product ended up weighing 12-13 ounces and was just under $4 to mail within the US. \u00a0One went to Canada for about $11 and two went further to the U.K. & Australia for nearly $17 each!\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1360474245375_5729\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/sad.gif\" style=\"line-height: 1.231;\" \/><\/span>\u00a0 Even still, I only spent about $75 mailing, since we have so many to hand deliver, so I wasn't too bothered by the International ones costing a fortune.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I'm super excited to give these to friends! \u00a0Really proud of myself, but definitely glad to be done! \u00a0I lost track of the number of hours I worked on them (weeks!) and also of the cost (surely more than I'd like to know, so I'm happy to remain ignorant about it), but I do think they were worth all the effort. \u00a0I saved one to keep and will hopefully remember to bring it to Mexico to include in our pro photos.<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> Wow, these are amazing!! You can tell a lot of time and effort went into these and they are very personalized!\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"day_ner@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"70.75.1.73","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1342726347,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-258078.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"RNtoBe","Id":258078,"Name":"RNtoBe","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":72470,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4355a084f0a34fce7445a542c39df18c","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Looks very nice. Great job!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1719878,"PostDate":1360707916,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Looks very nice. Great job!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"Anastasia_veronica@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"173.35.108.224","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1350333325,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-261393.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Dvhtu","Id":261393,"Name":"Dvhtu","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":72470,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"3099fe008009a408eab7f5581e5c7735","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Great job!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1720844,"PostDate":1360874051,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Great job!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jamlove24@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"23.24.145.81","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1359511337,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265358.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"DiggityDawn","Id":265358,"Name":"DiggityDawn","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":72470,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4c91593f66ebec4c41aa0420bdb55b16","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Everything came out great.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1729343,"PostDate":1362507134,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Everything came out great.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"fenikjo@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1353116151,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-262441.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"fenikjo","Id":262441,"Name":"fenikjo","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":72470,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f631a04945294908ed11be1c90ed4c7f","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Those are amazing, thanks for sharing!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1729984,"PostDate":1362593251,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Those are amazing, thanks for sharing!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"stacysorenson00@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1332967551,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-253321.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"stacysorenson00","Id":253321,"Name":"stacysorenson00","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":72470,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"06310b78a25f86b0706c294447faa1de","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I love the way they came out! So different from the MIB I usually see. They look super cute!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1730109,"PostDate":1362605514,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I love the way they came out! So different from the MIB I usually see. They look super cute!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"lyna_89_07@mugglenet.com","IpAddress":"172.8.174.118","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1362357491,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.steve